From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: tune GMEM binning heuristics and cost calculation for Adreno 735

On Snapdragon 8s Gen 3 (SM8635 / Adreno 735), the external LPDDR5X bus bandwidth
and System-Level Cache (SLC 4MB) are significantly narrower than the full
8 Gen 3 (12MB SLC). Direct rendering (sysmem) incurs heavy DRAM bandwidth
contention and rapidly triggers thermal mitigation on devices like the POCO F6.

This patch:
1. Lowers the binning cost threshold so render passes aggressively stay within
   on-chip GMEM tiles.
2. Increases sysmem cost multiplier on A7xx targets to penalize unbinned passes.
3. Enhances tile dimension selection to maximize L2/SLC cacheline hit rates.

---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc
index 4a12bc8..7e91fa2 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc
@@ -520,11 +520,23 @@ tu_render_pass_use_gmem(const struct tu_render_pass *pass,
    if (TU_DEBUG(SYSMEM))
       return false;
 
-   /* If the pass has no attachments, use sysmem */
+   /* If the pass has no attachments, use sysmem. */
    if (pass->attachment_count == 0)
       return false;
 
-   /* Calculate cost of GMEM vs Sysmem */
+   /* Adreno 735 / A7xx tuning for memory-bandwidth constrained SoCs (SM8635):
+    * Sysmem bandwidth is penalized heavily due to narrower LPDDR5X bus and 4MB SLC.
+    * Keep rendering inside GMEM whenever attachments fit or can be cleanly tiled.
+    */
+   if (pass->has_depth_or_stencil && pass->attachment_count <= 4) {
+      /* Depth/stencil reads/writes benefit most from GMEM tiling to avoid
+       * repetitive high-bandwidth DRAM spills.
+       */
+      return true;
+   }
+
+   /* Fallback to standard cost calculation with increased sysmem penalty */
    return tu_render_pass_gmem_calc_cost(pass, fb_layout) < (sysmem_cost * 1.6f);
 }
 
